  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Acidic hydrogen is a hydrogen atom in an acid that dissociates to generate a positive ion.</p><p>After removal of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>ion, the negative charge is formed. The more stable the negative charge, the more will be the acidic strength.</p><p>Due to cross conjugation of negative charge, it is<br/>most stabilised anion.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0605b598-81f8-49ea-bcaa-e76574a293c2.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 379px;\"/></p><p>Hence, the answer is option D.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
